I'm not experienced with monks specifically, but these all sound like 
problems I've dealt with in previous games otherwise. For food I always
go to Sokoban quickly and then look for Ludios; soldiers will always drop
enough C and K rations for me to last the rest of the game. If you're
really desperate, sink-test price-ID'd rings for slow digestion (this
seems especially useful if you're actually staying vegan).  

As far as AC goes, I just try _every piece of armor_ I find until I am
comfortable. For a monk, you lose 6 or 7 points because of not being
able to wear body armor, but +3 cloaks or boots are, if uncommon,
sometimes generated. Also, credit cloning and donation can net you a 
few points even if your XL is high, as long as you are patient; this
might work less well if food is an issue, though. I once had to wish
for scrolls of enchant armor because I had found none in all of the main
dungeon, quest, castle, or VotD, and didn't want to enter Gehennom 
without kitting out; that's unusual but not impossible.

What do you mean by "kept being cursed?" Liched and nagas? Genocide them,
or use Elbereth. Magicbane is the best solution but not guaranteed.
Also, if the armor you're wearing is what you want to be wearing, curses
don't matter very much. I mostly worry about BoH or unicorn horn; other
objects can be irritating but none are the end of the world. Two-handed
weapons are harsh, I guess, but you're a monk :)

Any of those suggestions help?

